{"updated":"2026-10-24T16:54:44.962Z","warnings":[{"country":"united-kingdom","level":2,"type":"Wind","event":"Yellow wind warning","headline":"Storm Boelo will bring a very windy and wet spell this weekend with some disruption likely across parts of northern UK. : UPDATED","description":"Information on update: Warning extended further south across northern England and into north Wales. . Strong winds will spread across northern parts of the UK during Saturday afternoon, combining with spells of heavy rain. Initially strong southerly winds will affect parts of Scotland before more widespread and even stronger westerly winds develop later on Saturday. Very windy conditions will then persist overnight and through much of Sunday before gradually easing from the southwest later. Gusts of 55-65 mph are likely widely with some coastal and exposed areas potentially seeing gusts of 70-80 mph or more, these strongest gusts most likely across Scotland and the far north of England. \n\nFo","instruction":"Prepare to protect your property and people from injury. Check for loose items outside your home and plan how you could secure them. Items include: bins, garden furniture, trampolines, tents, sheds, and fences.\n\nPeople cope better with power cuts when they have prepared for them in advance. It's easy to do; consider gathering torches and batteries, a mobile phone power pack and other essential ite","sender":"UK Met Office","web":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","onset":"2026-10-24T11:00:00.000Z","expires":"2026-10-25T21:00:00.000Z","areas":["Central, Tayside & Fife | East Midlands | Grampian | Highlands & Eilean Siar | North East England | North West England | Orkney & Shetland | Strathclyde | SW Scotland, Lothian Borders | Wales | West Midlands | Yorkshire & Humber"],"polys":[[[-4.92,52.75,-4.96,52.8,-4.96,52.96,-4.93,53.07,-4.76,53.36,-4.65,53.44,-3.83,53.83,-3.77,53.91,-3.77,53.99,-3.85,54.14,-4.05,54.33,-4.33,54.5,-4.54,54.55,-4.85,5